A custom-made website is a website built specifically using code according to the customer's or company's requirements.

Instead of selecting a ready-made template, the developer designs and develops the website structure, features, frontend, and backend.

Example

Suppose a hospital wants a Chronic Kidney Disease (CKD) Prediction Website.

The custom website can be built like this:

| Part       | Technology                | Purpose                              |
| ---------- | ------------------------- | ------------------------------------ |
| Frontend   | HTML, CSS, JavaScript     | User interface                       |
| Backend    | Flask / Django / FastAPI  | Handles user requests                |
| ML Model   | `finalized_model_ckd.sav` | Predicts CKD                         |
| Database   | MySQL / PostgreSQL        | Stores user or prediction data       |
| Deployment | Cloud server              | Makes the website publicly available |


